 **Total scenarios:** 21
 
+## Voyage 2: DOM-identity preservation (browser acceptance fix)
+
+**Product defect:** The external browser acceptance suite (Cypress) fails 4 scenarios with "element has detached from DOM". The app's `render()` function destroys and rebuilds the entire todo list (`list.innerHTML = ''`) on every state change. A real browser holds element references across command chains; when the node is replaced, those references become stale.
+
+**Spec written:**
+- `features/dom-identity.feature` — 4 scenarios covering DOM-identity preservation on toggle, toggle-all, and edit-save
+- `features/support/steps.js` — added capture/assertion steps for DOM node identity checks
+
+**Root cause in `js/app.js`:** The `render()` function at line ~119 does `list.innerHTML = ''` then recreates all `<li>` elements. The fix is to mutate existing nodes in place: when toggling a todo, find its `<li>`, toggle the class and checkbox state, do NOT rebuild the list. Only full re-renders (add/remove) should touch the list structure.
+
+**Total scenarios:** 28 (24 passing, 4 failing — the 4 new ones pin the defect)
+
 **Implementation plan (for QM/Crew):**
 - `index.html` at project root, adapted from `assets/app-template.index.html` (remove template comments, update paths to `node_modules/` CSS)
 - `js/app.js` at project root — single-file vanilla JS implementation
diff --git a/features/dom-identity.feature b/features/dom-identity.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..98f1f8e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/dom-identity.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: DOM identity preservation
+  As a user interacting with the todo list
+  When I toggle a todo or perform other state-changing actions
+  The existing DOM elements must remain attached to the document
+  So that browser-driven interactions (which hold element references across commands)
+  do not break with "element has detached from DOM" errors
+
+  Rule: Toggling a todo preserves the <li> node identity
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle checkbox does not replace the todo <li> element
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user captures the DOM identity of the first todo
+      And the user toggles the first todo
+      Then the first todo <li> element must still be the same DOM node
+      And the first todo should be completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle checkbox on a completed todo does not replace the <li> element
+      Given the user has created a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user captures the DOM identity of the first todo
+      And the user toggles the first todo
+      Then the first todo <li> element must still be the same DOM node
+      And the first todo should not be completed
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all preserves <li> node identities
+
+    Scenario: Clicking toggle-all does not replace any todo <li> elements
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user captures the DOM identity of all todos
+      And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todo <li> elements must still be the same DOM nodes
+      And all todos should be completed
+
+  Rule: Editing a todo preserves the <li> node identity
+
+    Scenario: Saving an edit does not replace the todo <li> element
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user captures the DOM identity of the first todo
+      And the user double-clicks the first todo label
+      And the user types "Buy soy milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter in the edit input
+      Then the first todo <li> element must still be the same DOM node
+      And the first todo should have title "Buy soy milk"
diff --git a/features/support/steps.js b/features/support/steps.js
index ba23e0b..e356a85 100644
--- a/features/support/steps.js
+++ b/features/support/steps.js
@@ -374,3 +374,50 @@ Then('the {string} filter link should not be selected', function (name) {
     throw new Error(`Expected "${name}" filter link to NOT be selected`);
   }
 });
+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// DOM identity preservation steps
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+When('the user captures the DOM identity of the first todo', function () {
+  const li = todoItems.call(this)[0];
+  if (!li) throw new Error('No todo items found to capture');
+  this._capturedFirstLi = li;
+});
+
+When('the user captures the DOM identity of all todos', function () {
+  const items = todoItems.call(this);
+  if (!items.length) throw new Error('No todo items found to capture');
+  this._capturedAllLis = items.slice();
+});
+
+Then('the first todo <li> element must still be the same DOM node', function () {
+  if (!this._capturedFirstLi) throw new Error('No DOM identity was captured for the first todo');
+  const currentItems = todoItems.call(this);
+  if (!currentItems.length) throw new Error('No todo items found after action');
+  if (currentItems[0] !== this._capturedFirstLi) {
+    throw new Error(
+      'DOM identity violation: the first todo <li> was replaced after the action. '
+      + 'The app must mutate the existing node in place, not rebuild the list.'
+    );
+  }
+});
+
+Then('all todo <li> elements must still be the same DOM nodes', function () {
+  if (!this._capturedAllLis) throw new Error('No DOM identities were captured for the todos');
+  const currentItems = todoItems.call(this);
+  if (currentItems.length !== this._capturedAllLis.length) {
+    throw new Error(
+      `DOM identity violation: expected ${this._capturedAllLis.length} todo items, found ${currentItems.length}. `
+      + 'The app must mutate existing nodes in place, not rebuild the list.'
+    );
+  }
+  for (var i = 0; i < currentItems.length; i++) {
+    if (currentItems[i] !== this._capturedAllLis[i]) {
+      throw new Error(
+        `DOM identity violation: todo <li> at index ${i} was replaced after the action. `
+        + 'The app must mutate existing nodes in place, not rebuild the list.'
+      );
+    }
+  }
+});
